            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107708",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "krb5: krb5: Denial of Service via malformed PAC in S4U2Proxy requests"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "MIT krb5 through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in the KDC's get_pac_princ_with_realm() that returns success while leaving the client principal NULL on malformed names. A malicious or compromised cross-realm trusted KDC can send an S4U2Proxy request with a PAC carrying a malformed client name to crash krb5kdc and deny authentication."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-107708",
