              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vul ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: zlib1g\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091)\nzlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|zlib1g||[CVE-2026-85091](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-85091)|\n\nzlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.76.0"
        }
